{title: Let Your Face Shine}
{subtitle: Psalms 80:3–4}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 85}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Bb/D] | [Eb] |
| [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]Shepherd of Israel, please [Bbmaj7/D]hear us now
[Eb]You lead Joseph like a flock [Bb]
Enthroned upon the cherubim [Dm7]
[Bbmaj7/D]Shine forth [Eb]from your holy [Bb]ground
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Before Ep[Gm]hraim, Benjamin, Manas[Dm]seh
[Eb]Stir up your great [Bb]might
Come and [Gm]save us from the [Dm]deep
Re[Eb]store us in the [Bb]light
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Restore us, O God
Let your face shine [Dm]on us
That we may be [Eb]saved
Restore us, [F]O [Bb]God
Let your face shine [Dm]on us
That we may be [Eb]saved
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Bb]LORD God of hosts, how long
[Dm]Will your anger smolder
[Eb]Against the prayer of your people
Waiting for the word
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Restore us, O [Bb]God
Let your face shine [Dm]on us
That we may be [Eb]saved
Restore us, [F]O [Bb]God
Let your face shine [Dm]on us
That we may be [Eb]saved
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Gm]Bread of tears and measure cups
[Dm]We have drunk them [Eb]all [Bb]
[Gm]Strife among our neigh[Dm]bors
[Eb]Enemies laugh and call
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Restore us, O [Bb]God
Let your face shine [Dm]on us
That we may be [Eb]saved
Restore us, [F7sus4]O [Bb]God
Let your face shine [Dm]on us
That we may be [Eb]saved [Ebsus2]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Bb]Let your face shine [Dm]on us
[Eb]That we may be saved
{end_of_verse}
